{"title":"2026 INMO Problems","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problems\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problems</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Problem_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Problem_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Problem_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Problem_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Problem_5\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 5</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Problem_6\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 6</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h1><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problems\">Problems</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_INMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problems\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h1>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_1\">Problem 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_INMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/a/1ba1ea2ff1caf77831140b0a5972314412f47af1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_1, x_2, x_3, \\ldots$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"97\" height=\"11\" /> be a sequence of positive integers defined as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/d/2dd241834905de5246fcbb2444ed65f963fccbce.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_1 = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"50\" height=\"14\" /> and for each <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/7/897470a282b6b85fa5221eacd41369b9a157f491.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\ge 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/a/6/da6821383bad74988bdb3845a6cea48b40aea81f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x_{n+1}=x_n+\\lfloor\\sqrt{x_n}\\rfloor.\\]\" width=\"156\" height=\"18\" /> Determine all positive integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> for which there exists some <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/0/340797a8fa9f1a06b10ce9e764998830b15ca755.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n\\ge1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"14\" /> for which <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/2/30214ba5d940687b09852b6db27ada82fead34b9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_n = m^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"69\" height=\"20\" />. (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/6/06681f5b345750104366c512078960fee8d81b49.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\lfloor x \\rfloor$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"23\" height=\"19\" /> denotes the greatest integer less than or equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> for every real <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />.)\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_INMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2026 INMO Problems/Problem 1\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_2\">Problem 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_INMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/6/e36ef566319486bfd69d5d0f4ea49c8bf8f01058.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f:\\mathbb{N}\\rightarrow\\mathbb{N}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"82\" height=\"18\" /> satisfy the following condition: for each <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/4/fd479012b79b5a10a93e25990a18efbe28ba6343.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k&gt;2026$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"72\" height=\"15\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/2/81232ecd8d9e4b5c0f24a00dabec238068f26de9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(k)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"33\" height=\"18\" /> equals the maximum number of times a number appears among <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/4/f944272089a25967bcbf73328f79f92cf199dc93.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(1), f(2), \\ldots, f(k-1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"185\" height=\"20\" />. Prove that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/1/b/21b59c37d1c83efdab2f3021d5f4f0f3e844eac9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(n)=f(n+f(n))$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"156\" height=\"20\" /> for infinitely many <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/4/a64508262bb2272e129bd59c31142b17e78b6ad3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n\\in\\mathbb{N}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"48\" height=\"15\" />, given <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/e/a1e6cd0e4103015efba12e0fc4291f012b467eaa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathbb{N}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> denotes the set of positive integers.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_INMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2026 INMO Problems/Problem 2\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_3\">Problem 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_INMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> be an acute-angled scalene triangle with circumcircle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/3/913e49ea63c6c130bb8d9d1c3556b052ecc404f8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Gamma$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"14\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> be the midpoint of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> the midpoint of minor arc <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/8/c/28cc93fbfb5ed16e87ce30594bc806a6094fe106.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\widehat{BC}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"20\" /> of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/3/913e49ea63c6c130bb8d9d1c3556b052ecc404f8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Gamma$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"14\" />. Points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/6/9866e3a998d628ba0941eb4fea0666ac391d149a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"16\" height=\"18\" /> lie of segments <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/7/a179ff2638e4799cadd820db205c2beff6299ce9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> respectively, such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/2/9a293135ae070917eb8797fb6f646726a4ec6fb7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BP=BN$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"86\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/4/b/b4bbca6cd8ae5d8d5784309e8a9056ba43c656a1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CQ=CN$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"86\" height=\"18\" />. Point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/e/dfea10d2e3c5fb78b74c2fa32425f21dcf6d9042.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$K\\neq N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"59\" height=\"18\" /> lies on line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/a/9aafc7e3cc1eafce5e16d3a45250eeda7b1a6526.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AN$\" width=\"30\" height=\"13\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/6/1f6e9cbd69e0d941a61dd38e089022e9a2bea880.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$MK=MN$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"99\" height=\"14\" />. Show that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/1/ef1c61197c83fce364174e9a1331dd98eefdc703.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\angle PKQ=90^{\\circ}.\\]\" width=\"111\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_INMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2026 INMO Problems/Problem 3\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_4\">Problem 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_INMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Two integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> are called <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/e/ffeca844051443e0d040f5fdeba6709c1bd3f576.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$companions$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"99\" height=\"17\" /> if every prime number <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> either divides both or none of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" />. Determine all functions <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/1/19168394453481cde2f88478650ece0c31cea667.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f:\\mathbb{N}_0\\rightarrow\\mathbb{N}_0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"97\" height=\"18\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/d/82d0e714dd3855ef2e740b789ae984e1d7cd5f39.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(0)=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"67\" height=\"18\" /> and the numbers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/c/ddc1c01aff14a0adc5d879844db764de8eb5ce4c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(m)+n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"76\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/e/82e89c81d7ba2b4b59f4c17ae4d1e93a9b8da16b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(n)+m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"76\" height=\"20\" /> are companions for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/f/c6f50291897389d3e8d1b7e1547a4e35cc99d85a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m, n \\in \\mathbb{N}_0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"76\" height=\"15\" />, given <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/e/4/7e4cf2fcc5a9f81da799e684ca53afc52482886e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathbb{N}_0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"22\" height=\"17\" /> is the set of all non-negative integers.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_INMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2026 INMO Problems/Problem 4\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_5\">Problem 5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_INMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Three lines <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/0/390a98e511e94f47fd329ee4b45f700252855007.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$l_1, l_2, l_3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"57\" height=\"18\" /> form an acute-angled triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/5/2554b6496c3b678897e9b060ef00aa9f0a7d7ece.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> in the plane. Point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> lies in the interior of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/5/2554b6496c3b678897e9b060ef00aa9f0a7d7ece.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/9/d694fbb5f4343aa3478faa6f4af36dcca04a72da.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tau_{i}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"15\" height=\"13\" /> denote the transformation of the plane such that the image <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/9/dd9b5c0cb50b5159042cfdbfbe1efa704e871aa1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tau_{i} (X)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"46\" height=\"20\" /> of any point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/4/6a47ca0fe7cb276abc022af6ac88ddae1a9d6894.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> in the plane is the reflection of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/4/6a47ca0fe7cb276abc022af6ac88ddae1a9d6894.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/9/74949574eb3bb72bd595192b9685db088e6a44bd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$l_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"10\" height=\"15\" /> for each <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/f/f7fdf52e14b7bec6d3098d2108e3a4deec365250.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i\\in\\{1, 2, 3\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"92\" height=\"20\" />. Denote by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/a/a2a641c2fc406d7f5345d79d80623592bba6cc00.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_{ijk}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"33\" height=\"19\" /> the point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/e/96ea5570c307e3e1fb8ec14431dce2e3457c2051.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tau_{k} (\\tau_{j} (\\tau_{i} (P)))$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"103\" height=\"20\" /> for each permutation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/e/7/7e77ac2f68634e9d36db4e965bc2f8d52709c673.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(i, j, k)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"52\" height=\"18\" /> of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/f/dcfc6112a596558ea2b5c4d3009f082ec9763d21.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1,2,3)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"56\" height=\"18\" />. Prove that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/4/fd4e887f1d9eb6cc931de15c168da3f6d5947464.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_{123}, P_{132},P_{213},P_{231},P_{312},P_{321}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"236\" height=\"18\" /> are concyclic if and only if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is the orthocenter of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/5/2554b6496c3b678897e9b060ef00aa9f0a7d7ece.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_INMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2026 INMO Problems/Problem 5\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_6\">Problem 6</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_INMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 6\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Two decks <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/7/78792fe4680a164f537ea72a4f900e4471433c3b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$40$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> cards each are placed on a table at noon. Every minute thereafter, we pick the topmost cards of the decks, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/5/1a50f85686fe7cb27b1ae676014e18fc9e46e9bc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a\\in A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"45\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/9/9/999e49d223e45c4430a52817a56531e24d7bcb3e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b\\in B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"13\" />, and perform a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/8/7/287c274ed827e94952eebf82af7f16a15f5975da.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$duel$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"36\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>For any two cards <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/5/1a50f85686fe7cb27b1ae676014e18fc9e46e9bc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a\\in A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"45\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/4/2c4a5415d1e2419d839d8bd4d5045549c441bd4a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b \\in B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"13\" />, each time <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> duel, the outcome remains the same and is independent of other duels. A duel has three possible outcomes:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/3/7f3b4ea3b8abe9ced6095c7d75f207a1127ee843.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: 1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"7\" /> If a card wins, it is placed back on the top of its deck and the losing card is placed at the bottom of its deck.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/3/7f3b4ea3b8abe9ced6095c7d75f207a1127ee843.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: 1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"7\" /> If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> are evenly matched, they are both removed from their respective decks.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/3/7f3b4ea3b8abe9ced6095c7d75f207a1127ee843.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: 1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"7\" /> If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> do not interact with each other, then both are placed at the bottom of their respective decks.\n</p><p>The sequence of duels ends when both decks are empty, otherwise it goes on forever. Prove that either such a sequence of duels continues infinitely, or the sequence ends at most <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/9/509f7aafdacc5424492342c2b0d23ca9c2f177bc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$356$\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" /> hours after the first duel.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_INMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2026 INMO Problems/Problem 6\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_INMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_INMO\" title=\"2026 INMO\">2026 INMO</a></b> (<b><a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">Problems</a></b>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_INMO\" title=\"2025 INMO\">2025 INMO</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"34%\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_INMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2026 INMO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_INMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2026 INMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_INMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2026 INMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_INMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2026 INMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_INMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2026 INMO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_INMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2026 INMO Problems/Problem 6\">6</a>\n</td>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2027_INMO&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2027 INMO (page does